\newlabel{tab:mechanisms}{{14}{14}{Logged mechanism totals across the available C/D/E archives. Candidate and trial IDs are scoped to each archive; disposition labels are not independently verified queue membership. Metrics requiring descendant joins or verified fixed-energy, independent code-branch rewards remain blank; the separate logged-reward diagnostics appear in Table~\ref {tab:logged_calibration}}{table.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces State-level E-archive illustrations for the three motivating targets, selected by the deterministic rule in the text. Upper panels show pre-update probabilities; lower panels show the logged final selection score divided by the frontier score. Each point is positioned at the logged episode-end time; connecting lines only guide the eye. Zero-frontier records have an undefined multiplier and are omitted from the lower panels. Colors identify states within each target, not equivalent states across targets. Unequal mutation energy, possible posterior resets, and native save-event rewards limit interpretation. The selected source paths and exact plotted values accompany the figure.}}{15}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:posterior_cases}{{6}{15}{State-level E-archive illustrations for the three motivating targets, selected by the deterministic rule in the text. Upper panels show pre-update probabilities; lower panels show the logged final selection score divided by the frontier score. Each point is positioned at the logged episode-end time; connecting lines only guide the eye. Zero-frontier records have an undefined multiplier and are omitted from the lower panels. Colors identify states within each target, not equivalent states across targets. Unequal mutation energy, possible posterior resets, and native save-event rewards limit interpretation. The selected source paths and exact plotted values accompany the figure}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Logged candidate dispositions (left) and first failed trial flags in $P\tmspace  -\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rightarrow \tmspace  -\thinmuskip {.1667em}U\tmspace  -\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rightarrow \tmspace  -\thinmuskip {.1667em}R$ order (right), pooled within each archive arm. Exact counts accompany percentages. The candidate denominators are 1,326/1,992/726 for C/D/E; the trial denominators are 1,326/1,991/725. D and E each have one unmatched candidate, whose narrow segment is identified by the count. Passing $P/U/R$ does not establish code gain or durable queue membership. Provisional, converted, and expired outcomes have no validated lifecycle evidence and are not assigned zero rates.}}{15}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dispositions}{{7}{15}{Logged candidate dispositions (left) and first failed trial flags in $P\!\rightarrow \!U\!\rightarrow \!R$ order (right), pooled within each archive arm. Exact counts accompany percentages. The candidate denominators are 1,326/1,992/726 for C/D/E; the trial denominators are 1,326/1,991/725. D and E each have one unmatched candidate, whose narrow segment is identified by the count. Passing $P/U/R$ does not establish code gain or durable queue membership. Provisional, converted, and expired outcomes have no validated lifecycle evidence and are not assigned zero rates}{figure.7}{}}
