\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Saved token counters versus native terminal code coverage, with one marker per B--E archive (375 observations). Token usage is the saved prompt-plus-completion count, expressed in thousands; individual observations show the available dispersion without imposing a fitted efficiency frontier. Different targets have separate axes, and missing E--bftpd is omitted. AFLNet lacks a comparable saved counter and is not assigned a synthetic zero. Horizons and build provenance are not matched, and final counters may lag the event stream. This is a descriptive cost--coverage view, not reconciled billing or a cost-matched causal comparison.}}{16}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cost}{{8}{16}{Saved token counters versus native terminal code coverage, with one marker per B--E archive (375 observations). Token usage is the saved prompt-plus-completion count, expressed in thousands; individual observations show the available dispersion without imposing a fitted efficiency frontier. Different targets have separate axes, and missing E--bftpd is omitted. AFLNet lacks a comparable saved counter and is not assigned a synthetic zero. Horizons and build provenance are not matched, and final counters may lag the event stream. This is a descriptive cost--coverage view, not reconciled billing or a cost-matched causal comparison}{figure.8}{}}
